          "title": "A clear goal",
          "text": "Algorithmic thinking plans a solution as steps.\n\nState what must be achieved.\n\nCheck that the steps reach that goal.\n\nChallenge: Why state the goal before writing steps?\n\nThe goal defines what counts as a correct result."
        },
        {
          "id": "f2",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Input, process, output",
          "text": "Identify data entering the algorithm.\n\nIdentify operations on the data.\n\nIdentify the result to communicate.\n\nChallenge: Name the inputs for calculating hire cost.\n\nThe number of hours and the hourly rate."
        },
        {
          "id": "f3",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Order matters",
          "text": "A value must be available before use.\n\nCalculate before displaying the result.\n\nChanging order can change behaviour.\n\nChallenge: What is wrong with printing total first?\n\nThe total has not yet been calculated from the inputs."
        },
        {
          "id": "f4",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Remove ambiguity",
          "text": "Instructions need clear actions and quantities.\n\nAvoid words such as some or enough.\n\nSpecify what happens in each case.\n\nChallenge: Rewrite Add some bonus points precisely.\n\nAdd 5 bonus points to score is one precise example."
        },
